{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/docset at 24eaaf2e37c79b947addd0a0cbc269e0002d0ad8 on request/docset-citation-integrity.\n\nThe citation gate now judges what a basis can do rather than only that it resolves. Five fatal classes: unresolvable, not an artifact, retired, a path succession cannot maintain, and a commit that is not a full canonical object id. Stale but live reports and never fails, because every artifact at every core package is stale today and failing on stale would redden the whole set for behaving as designed.\n\nClassifyCitation takes primitives rather than workroom types so every branch is exercisable without a workroom; the retired and unresolvable cases are otherwise tested only by whatever the live log happens to hold. The gate calls the same function, so there is one set of rules and not a copy in the test.\n\nThe known-failing list bounds the rollout. Anything new fails immediately, a recorded defect that changes shape fails, and a recorded entry that has stopped failing fails too — the last is what makes it shrink rather than accumulate.\n\nThe list is generated by the same code path the gate reads, so the two cannot disagree about what is failing or why, and regenerating it is a test guarded by an environment variable — the diff is the review.\n\nMutation-verified: dropping the shrink rule, accepting a changed defect, and accepting an abbreviated commit each fail the focused tests. The third initially did not, because the table had no non-canonical commit in it; the class was untested until the mutation said so, which is the argument for mutating rather than counting tests.","body":{"branch":"request/docset-citation-integrity","commit":"24eaaf2e37c79b947addd0a0cbc269e0002d0ad8","head":"24eaaf2e37c79b947addd0a0cbc269e0002d0ad8","path":"internal/docset"}}